1	<!DOCTYPE html>
2	<html lang="en">
3	<head>
4	<meta charset="UTF-8">
5	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
6	<title>mbarrier State and Operations</title>
7	<link rel="stylesheet" href="../viz-base.css">
8	<script src="../viz-base.js"></script>
9	<style>
10	  body { padding: 20px 28px; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; }
11	
12	  .struct-section {
13	    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px;
14	    margin-bottom: 18px;
15	  }
16	
17	  .struct-card {
18	    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
19	    padding: 16px 18px; background: var(--surface);
20	    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.04);
21	  }
22	  .struct-card h3 {
23	    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px;
24	    color: #1e293b;
25	  }
26	
27	  .field-row {
28	    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
29	    padding: 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
30	  }
31	  .field-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
32	  .field-name {
33	    font-family: 'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace; font-size: 11.5px;
34	    font-weight: 600; color: #3b82f6; min-width: 120px;
35	  }
36	  .field-desc {
37	    font-size: 12px; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5;
38	  }
39	
40	  .obj-visual {
41	    display: flex; gap: 0; margin: 10px 0 6px; justify-content: center;
42	  }
43	  .obj-slot {
44	    padding: 10px 10px; text-align: center; border: 2px solid;
45	    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; min-width: 80px;
46	  }
47	  .obj-slot:first-child { border-radius: 8px 0 0 8px; }
48	  .obj-slot:last-child  { border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
49	  .obj-slot.s-phase    { border-color: #94a3b8; background: #f1f5f9; color: #334155; }
50	  .obj-slot.s-pending  { border-color: #94a3b8; background: #f1f5f9; color: #334155; }
51	  .obj-slot.s-expected { border-color: #94a3b8; background: #f1f5f9; color: #334155; }
52	  .obj-slot.s-tx       { border-color: #94a3b8; background: #f1f5f9; color: #334155; }
53	  .obj-slot .slot-label {
54	    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 600; opacity: .7;
55	    font-family: 'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace;
56	    margin-bottom: 2px;
57	  }
58	
59	  .api-table {
60	    width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;
61	    font-size: 12px;
62	  }
63	  .api-table th {
64	    text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px;
65	    background: #f8fafc; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
66	    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #64748b;
67	    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .5px;
68	  }
69	  .api-table td {
70	    padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
71	    vertical-align: top;
72	  }
73	  .api-table tr:hover { background: #f8fafc; }
74	  .api-name {
75	    font-family: 'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace; font-size: 11.5px;
76	    font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;
77	  }
78	  .api-name { color: #1e293b; }
79	  .api-role {
80	    font-size: 11.5px; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5;
81	  }
82	  .api-effect {
83	    font-size: 11px; color: #64748b; line-height: 1.5;
84	    font-family: 'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace;
85	  }
86	
87	  .tag {
88	    display: inline-block; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 3px;
89	    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600;
90	    font-family: 'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace;
91	  }
92	  .tag { background: #f1f5f9; color: #64748b; }
93	
94	  .note-bar {
95	    padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px;
96	    background: #fffbeb; border: 1px solid #fde68a;
97	    font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: #78350f;
98	    margin-top: 14px;
99	  }
100	  .note-bar strong { color: #c2410c; }
101	
102	  /* ── Clickable data structure slots ─────────────────────── */
103	  .obj-slot { cursor: pointer; transition: opacity .3s, transform .15s; }
104	  .obj-slot:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
105	  .obj-slot.slot-active { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.12); }
106	  .field-row { transition: opacity .3s; }
107	  .field-row.field-dim { opacity: 0.2; }
108	
109	  @media(max-width:800px) { .struct-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
110	</style>
111	</head>
112	<body>
113	  <h1>mbarrier State and Operations</h1>
114	
115	  <div class="struct-section">
116	    <div class="struct-card">
117	      <h3>mbarrier object (64-bit, in shared memory)</h3>
118	      <div class="obj-visual">
119	        <div class="obj-slot s-phase"><div class="slot-label">phase parity</div>0 or 1</div>
120	        <div class="obj-slot s-pending"><div class="slot-label">pending arrival<br>count</div>arrivals left</div>
121	        <div class="obj-slot s-expected"><div class="slot-label">expected arrival<br>count</div>expected total</div>
122	        <div class="obj-slot s-tx"><div class="slot-label">tx-count</div>bytes pending</div>
123	      </div>
124	      <div class="field-row">
125	        <span class="field-name">phase parity</span>
126	        <span class="field-desc">The parity of the current phase. It alternates between 0 and 1 whenever the barrier advances.</span>
127	      </div>
128	      <div class="field-row">
129	        <span class="field-name">pending arrival count</span>
130	        <span class="field-desc">The arrivals still required before the current phase can complete.</span>
131	      </div>
132	      <div class="field-row">
133	        <span class="field-name">expected arrival count</span>
134	        <span class="field-desc">The number of arrivals required in each phase, set by <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">init</code>.</span>
135	      </div>
136	      <div class="field-row">
137	        <span class="field-name">tx-count</span>
138	        <span class="field-desc">Bytes of asynchronous transfer still outstanding. <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">arrive.expect_tx</code> increases this count; hardware decreases it as transfers complete.</span>
139	      </div>
140	    </div>
141	
142	    <div class="struct-card">
143	      <h3>Phase Completion Condition</h3>
144	      <div style="padding:12px 14px;background:#f8fafc;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:10px;font-family:'SF Mono','Fira Code',monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:2;text-align:center;">
145	        pending_arrival_count == 0<br>
146	        <strong style="color:#1e293b;">&amp;&amp;</strong><br>
147	        tx_count == 0
148	      </div>
149	      <div class="field-desc" style="line-height:1.65;">
150	        The current phase completes only after <strong style="color:#1e293b;">all expected arrivals have occurred</strong> and <strong style="color:#1e293b;">all registered asynchronous transfer bytes have completed</strong>.
151	        The barrier then advances atomically to the next phase and restores the pending arrival count from the expected arrival count.
152	      </div>
153	    </div>
154	  </div>
155	
156	  <div class="struct-card" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
157	    <h3>Core APIs</h3>
158	    <table class="api-table">
159	      <thead>
160	        <tr><th>Instruction</th><th>Role</th><th>Effect on mbarrier</th></tr>
161	      </thead>
162	      <tbody>
163	        <tr>
164	          <td><span class="api-name">mbarrier.init</span> <span class="tag">setup</span></td>
165	          <td class="api-role">Set the number of arrivals required in each phase</td>
166	          <td class="api-effect">phase=0, expected_arrival_count=count, pending_arrival_count=count, tx_count=0</td>
167	        </tr>
168	        <tr>
169	          <td><span class="api-name">mbarrier.arrive</span> <span class="tag">producer</span></td>
170	          <td class="api-role">Thread reports an arrival to the barrier</td>
171	          <td class="api-effect">pending_arrival_count -= 1</td>
172	        </tr>
173	        <tr>
174	          <td><span class="api-name">mbarrier.arrive.expect_tx</span> <span class="tag">participant</span></td>
175	          <td class="api-role">Arrive and declare the expected asynchronous transfer bytes</td>
176	          <td class="api-effect">pending_arrival_count -= 1, tx_count += byte_count</td>
177	        </tr>
178	        <tr>
179	          <td><span class="api-name">tcgen05.commit</span> <span class="tag">producer</span></td>
180	          <td class="api-role">Track asynchronous tcgen05 operations previously issued by this thread</td>
181	          <td class="api-effect">The system performs one arrive(count=1) after completion</td>
182	        </tr>
183	        <tr>
184	          <td><span class="api-name">T.ptx.mbarrier.try_wait</span> <span class="tag">consumer</span></td>
185	          <td class="api-role">Wait for the requested phase to complete</td>
186	          <td class="api-effect">Does not modify barrier state; retries internally and returns after completion</td>
187	        </tr>
188	      </tbody>
189	    </table>
190	  </div>
191	
192	  <div class="note-bar">
193	    <strong>Three update paths:</strong> (1) <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">mbarrier.arrive</code> directly reduces the pending arrival count.
194	    (2) <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">arrive.expect_tx</code> arrives and increases tx-count; when the associated TMA copy finishes, hardware reduces tx-count through <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">complete_tx</code>.
195	    (3) <code style="font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;">tcgen05.commit...arrive::one</code> makes the system report one arrival after the preceding asynchronous tcgen05 operations complete.
196	  </div>
197	<script>
198	(function () {
199	  var slots = document.querySelectorAll('.obj-slot');
200	  var fieldRows = document.querySelectorAll('.field-row');
201	
202	  slots.forEach(function (slot, i) {
203	    slot.addEventListener('click', function () {
204	      var isActive = slot.classList.contains('slot-active');
205	      /* Clear all */
206	      slots.forEach(function (s) { s.classList.remove('slot-active'); });
207	      fieldRows.forEach(function (r) { r.classList.remove('field-dim'); });
208	
209	      if (!isActive) {
210	        slot.classList.add('slot-active');
211	        fieldRows.forEach(function (r, j) {
212	          if (j !== i) r.classList.add('field-dim');
213	        });
214	      }
215	    });
216	  });
217	})();
218	</script>
219	</body>
220	</html>
